The ability to kill monsters quickly -- by some means
or another -- is pretty much mandatory to success, as
near as I can tell.

It doesn't really matter exactly how you do it, and 
that's going to depend on role.  Samurai whack monsters
upside the head with Excalibur and a katana.  Rangers 
use multishot projectiles.  Monks embed their palm 
print three inches deep in the monster's forehead.  
Wizards use magic missile.  Late-game Tourists have 
their choice between two-weapon combat, projectiles,
*or* attack spells, whichever they prefer.  Pacifists
use strong pets.  Whatever.  But every character has 
to have some way to quickly accomplish their foes'
deaths.  It's required.

Otherwise they kill you, and also you don't get
much really good loot -- not just all the really
good wands but also potions (almost all of the 
inputs for alchemy come from inventory that the 
monsters will consume themselves if you leave 
them alive too long) and polyfodder (not least, 
unicorn horns) and various other important things.

Plus, at some point you start running into 
monsters that can heal themselves via monster
spells.  If you can't kill them quickly, you
can't kill them at all.

